{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented in worktree `fix-dbac-codequality-desc` at origin/main 5f618b3ccff. Diff is 2 files (the certified `file_impact` set exactly): `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code_quality.md` and the regenerated `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json`.\n\nThe plan's exact replacement sentence landed verbatim; AC3 parses the YAML and asserts equality, so the line-wrap cannot hide a mismatch.\n\nTwo implementation findings worth recording, neither of which changes the certified plan:\n\n1. **The replacement sentence contains `prompt: code-quality`, and a colon-space sequence is illegal inside an unquoted YAML plain scalar.** Writing it unquoted made the whole prompt unparseable — `regenerate-index` died with `invalid prompt front-matter: mapping values are not allowed here` at the `prompt:` token. The value has to be a quoted scalar.\n\n2. **The repo requires the committed front matter to be a canonical fixed point.** `tests/unit/test_prompt_front_matter.py::test_built_in_prompt_round_trips_canonically` asserts `write_front_matter(*split_raw(file)) == file`. A hand-written double-quoted scalar fails that even though it parses correctly; the canonicalizer emits single-quoted. The file was therefore produced by running `write_front_matter` over the parsed meta/body rather than by hand-editing, which makes it canonical by construction.\n\nCriteria status: AC1-AC9 and AC11 PASS (script at `.rebar/scratch/ac-dbac.sh`, exits 0). AC10 PASS — `pytest tests/unit/test_prompt_index.py tests/unit/test_prompt_front_matter.py tests/unit/test_reviewer_prompt_hygiene.py` = 114 passed. AC12 (`make verify`) is running.\n\nNot yet committed or pushed."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793384587980091745,"uuid":"54313985-5277-44d9-bd27-cdeda2bac015"}